node_modules/
coverage/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.vitest/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Output of every `browser-inspector` run: screenshots, report.json, session journals — the page
# under test is somebody's application and what lands here is its data.
.scribe-devtools/

# Output of every `nx-angular-inspector` run: digests of somebody's workspace. Short on purpose —
# the path is printed on every line of stdout, and `.ws/projects.md` is 3 o200k tokens against 10
# for the long form. Needs the `.prettierignore` twin: one run of the tool would otherwise turn
# `prettier --check .` red.
.ws/

# The benchmark's raw results; RAPORT.md/WYNIKI.md/BUDGET.md are committed, the JSON behind them is not.
bench/out/

# What the @playwright/mcp server drops in the working directory (console logs, page snapshots) when
# it runs — during `npm run bench`, or from a `.vscode/mcp.json` / `.mcp.json` a human copied from the
# `.example` files for a manual comparison. Untracked AND unformatted: without the `.prettierignore`
# twin, one bench run turns `npm run verify` red.
.playwright-mcp/

# A live MCP config would put 4069 tokens of tool schemas into every agent request; the repository
# ships only the `.example` twins. A copy made for a manual comparison must not be committed.
.mcp.json
.vscode/mcp.json

# The portable zip IS tracked — every version lives in download/ (built by the pre-commit hook,
# deterministic bytes, .sha256 sidecar). A zip anywhere else is a stray build.
*-portable-*.zip
!download/*-portable-*.zip

# A read config carries the URLs, selectors and flows of the app it inspects — yours, not the
# template's. The negations must name their directories: a slash-less pattern matches at every depth.
read.config.*.json
!packages/*/fixtures/read.config.*.json
!examples/read.config.*.json
